msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:62
msgid "This section covers the question and answer pages of the site. Review it after changing the settings of easyQ, as it describes them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:65
msgid "the experts, editors, moderators and administrators of the site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:66
msgid "the editors, moderators and administrators of the site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:67
msgid "the moderators and administrators of the site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:68
msgid "the super administrators of the network"
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:69
msgid "the administrators of the site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:71
msgid "When you ask a question, write an answer or a comment, vote, or flag a post, we store it with your user account. Questions, answers and comments are public and show your user name and profile picture."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: who may see it, such as "the administrators of the site".
#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:73
#, php-format
msgid "Votes and flags are stored so that each counts only once; who cast them is visible only to %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:75
msgid "To prevent abuse, we also store the IP address from which a post was written or last changed, shortened by its last part."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:76
msgid "To prevent abuse, we also store the IP address from which a post was written or last changed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:79
msgid "If you post without an account, we store the name you enter, if any, and your email address only if you ask to be notified of answers or comments. We then send one request to confirm the address at most every hour; for that hour a hash of the address is kept, which WordPress removes within a day after that, not the address itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:82
msgid "If you have an account, your profile on the question and answer pages shows your user name, your points, your activity and the profile fields you fill in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:84
msgid "A profile picture you upload is stored in the media library of the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:90
msgid "Unless a profile picture was uploaded, the question and answer pages show the picture of the Gravatar service: an anonymized string created from the email address (also called a hash) is part of the address of the picture, and your browser loads it from Gravatar, which receives your IP address. The Gravatar service privacy policy is available here: https://automattic.com/privacy/."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:94
msgid "When you register, we store the time at which you accepted our terms and the text you accepted, as proof of your consent. This record stays with your user account as long as it exists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:99
msgid "Private messages are sent to the recipient by email and stored until the sender and the recipient have deleted them; only they can see them. You can choose in your account not to receive private messages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:100
msgid "Private messages are sent to the recipient by email and not stored on the site. You can choose in your account not to receive private messages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:103
msgid "Posts on the wall of a profile are public."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:106
msgid "We send you emails about answers and comments on your posts only if you ask for them; each of these emails contains a link to turn them off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:109
msgid "If you subscribe to our newsletter, you confirm the subscription with a link we send to your email address, and we store the time of your consent. You can unsubscribe at any time with the link in each newsletter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:112
msgid "If you send us a message with the feedback form, we receive it by email together with your name, your email address and your IP address. It is not stored on the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:115
msgid "Cookies on the question and answer pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:118
msgid "If you post without an account and agree to it, we set a cookie that lets you edit your posts later. It contains a random number and lasts for one year from your last post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:119
msgid "If you post without an account, we set a cookie that lets you edit your posts later. It contains a random number and lasts for one year from your last post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:124
msgid "If you log in on a question and answer page or close the notice for new visitors, we set a cookie so that the notice is not shown again. It contains no personal data and lasts for ten years."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:126
msgid "Views of questions are counted without cookies. So that a second view in a row does not count, a hash of your IP address is kept with the question for one hour, and WordPress removes it within a day after that; the address itself is not stored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:128
msgid "How long we keep the data of the question and answer pages"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: Number of days.
#: includes/privacy/class-policy-text.php:131
#, php-format
msgid "Questions, answers, comments, votes and profiles are kept until they are deleted. IP addresses are deleted after %d day; those counted to limit how often an action can be performed, by the daily clean-up after the hour they count for."
msgid_plural "Questions, answers, comments, votes and profiles are kept until they are deleted. IP addresses are deleted after %d days; those counted to limit how often an action can be performed, by the daily clean-up after the hour they count for."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

